WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:03.590
The booming steps echoed through the museum
corridors.

00:00:03.590 --> 00:00:10.040
Pharaohs, emperors, and Mongolian war leaders
all stood stock still as the terrified security

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:12.000
guard ran between them.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.719
Roger Pascal swung his flashlight this way
and that.

00:00:15.719 --> 00:00:21.769
The light glinted on the polished steel of
ancient weaponry: muskets, scimitars, and

00:00:21.769 --> 00:00:22.769
cannons.

00:00:22.769 --> 00:00:26.679
Exhibit after exhibit flashed past him as
he ran through the dark museum.

00:00:26.679 --> 00:00:31.340
There was no way it was real, no possible
way.

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:34.360
He was having a bad dream, that's all it was.

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:36.070
A bad dream.

00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:41.200
The shaking ground under his feet and the
marching rhythm of the impossibly heavy footsteps

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:44.550
behind him told him that it was real, alright.

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:49.700
It had just been a normal shift like any other,
just a regular night at the museum.

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:54.630
Roger had been sipping his coffee and listening
to the radio, when all of a sudden, he felt

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:57.059
his chair start rumbling beneath him.

00:00:57.059 --> 00:01:02.629
He put his coffee down on the table and watched
as it recoiled as the footsteps grew louder

00:01:02.629 --> 00:01:03.629
and closer.

00:01:03.629 --> 00:01:08.370
He’d got up to investigate and couldn’t
believe what he’d walked in on.

00:01:08.370 --> 00:01:12.759
Skidding around the corner, he tumbled into
a medieval suit of armor and sent it crashing

00:01:12.759 --> 00:01:14.370
across the floor.

00:01:14.370 --> 00:01:20.080
Chainmail helmet, gauntlets, all of it rattled
and crashed to the marble floor, echoing all

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:21.799
through the museum.

00:01:21.799 --> 00:01:26.620
Then there was a sudden deathly silence as
the footsteps stopped.

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:27.860
Roger didn’t breathe.

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:31.270
Then they started again, heading straight
towards him.

00:01:31.270 --> 00:01:36.460
It was all Roger could do to lie on his back
in front of a giant taxidermy eagle and point

00:01:36.460 --> 00:01:41.299
his flashlight at the doorway as the monstrous
figure of the stone soldier walked around

00:01:41.299 --> 00:01:44.039
the corner, musket in hand.

00:01:44.039 --> 00:01:45.039
*

00:01:45.039 --> 00:01:46.130
Woodstock, Vermont, 1995.

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:49.670
It was a normal day just like any other.

00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:54.510
The birds were singing in the trees, and there
was a gentle breeze blowing through.

00:01:54.510 --> 00:02:00.189
Nothing at all out of the ordinary, except,
of course, the statue that opened its eyes.

00:02:00.189 --> 00:02:05.560
The Civil War memorial had been a staple of
Woodstock for well over 100 years, a plinth

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:10.750
sitting in the middle of a park with a young
soldier on top of it, holding a musket peacefully

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:12.080
by his side.

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:16.680
The statue had watched over the town generation
after generation.

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:20.440
Except now its watching had become a little
more active.

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:23.480
It took several hours for anyone to notice.

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:29.130
Dog walkers went past listening to their Walkmans,
a banker sat on a bench opposite, deep in

00:02:29.130 --> 00:02:31.650
conversation on a giant brick phone.

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:36.500
It was only when a young child running after
her football looked up at the statue and saw

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:40.250
it looking back at her that things changed.

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:44.069
The girl's parents didn't listen to her, of
course; parents rarely do.

00:02:44.069 --> 00:02:47.180
But word quickly went around the girl's school.

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:51.909
Most of the time, the statue was totally still,
no movement in the eyes at all.

00:02:51.909 --> 00:02:56.760
But on occasion, when a group of kids gathered
around it and talked to it enough, the statue

00:02:56.760 --> 00:03:00.640
seemed to look down at them as if it was listening.

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:01.660
But that was it.

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:06.129
No grown-ups were particularly interested
in what the children were saying, and even

00:03:06.129 --> 00:03:10.900
a lot of the children who saw it went home,
concluding that they must have been imagining

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:11.900
things.

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:16.769
So six months went by without anyone really
paying the statue much attention.

00:03:16.769 --> 00:03:19.930
That was, until it fired its gun.

00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:24.950
In a quiet rural town, everyone hears a gunshot,
but for a long time, no one could work out

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:26.470
where it had come from.

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:31.280
Police gathered around the park, searching
all around where the weapon had been heard.

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:36.010
The only clue they could find was a small
hole in the wall of a shop across the street.

00:03:36.010 --> 00:03:40.510
A couple of officers joked that the shot must
have come from the statue itself.

00:03:40.510 --> 00:03:45.140
Everyone laughed it off except for a couple
of the school kids who were playing nearby.

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:49.520
Less than two weeks later, another shot rang
out in the middle of the night, and a group

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:53.859
of confused police officers rushed to the
park to investigate what had happened.

00:03:53.859 --> 00:03:58.400
The only thing they found was a dead bird
lying on the sidewalk, shot to death.

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:02.840
Again, the jokes went around the department
that it must have been the statue who did

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:08.610
it, except this time, the officers were all
laughing a little less enthusiastically.

00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:12.799
Without much crime going on in Woodstock,
Vermont, the department decided to take the

00:04:12.799 --> 00:04:18.139
shooting quite seriously, going so far as
to perform an autopsy on the dead pigeon.

00:04:18.139 --> 00:04:23.420
But when they cut the animal open and looked
at the wound inside its chest, they were filled

00:04:23.420 --> 00:04:27.060
with even more confusion than they were before.

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:31.240
It wasn't a conventional bullet lodged into
the bird's rib cage at all.

00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:35.759
It was perfectly round and made of what appeared
to be stone.

00:04:35.759 --> 00:04:39.150
But the next shot that rang out from the Memorial
Park was unmistakable.

00:04:39.150 --> 00:04:44.419
It was a weekend in the middle of the summer
vacation, so the park was full of families

00:04:44.419 --> 00:04:50.400
all sitting around having picnics, BBQs, and
staring up at the sky, watching the birds

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:52.030
circle lazily overhead.

00:04:52.030 --> 00:04:53.030
Bang!

00:04:53.030 --> 00:04:57.820
One of the pigeons exploded in a burst of
feathers and plummeted out of the sky, landing

00:04:57.820 --> 00:05:00.170
on the sidewalk in front of the whole town.

00:05:00.170 --> 00:05:05.449
In shock, all of the town's folk turned around
to see the stone statue down on one knee with

00:05:05.449 --> 00:05:07.430
his musket on his shoulder.

00:05:07.430 --> 00:05:12.260
The statue looked down at all of them, surprised
at the attention, then quickly got back to

00:05:12.260 --> 00:05:15.550
its feet and resumed its normal stance.

00:05:15.550 --> 00:05:18.639
Reports flooded all of the local papers and
news stations.

00:05:18.639 --> 00:05:23.390
The event was blamed on mass hysteria, a kind
of group hallucination where everyone was

00:05:23.390 --> 00:05:25.810
somehow sharing the same story.

00:05:25.810 --> 00:05:31.940
But the number of people coming forward with
the exact same account was irrefutable evidence.

00:05:31.940 --> 00:05:34.350
That's where the Foundation had to step in.

00:05:34.350 --> 00:05:42.300
In January 1996, containment procedures began,
and the statue was given the designation SCP-011.

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:46.639
Of course, a large contingent of agents suddenly
appearing in a small town would raise a lot

00:05:46.639 --> 00:05:50.790
of suspicion, so the Foundation had to move
very cautiously.

00:05:50.790 --> 00:05:55.880
One agent at a time, the Foundation established
itself in Woodstock and began to study the

00:05:55.880 --> 00:06:01.270
statue day in, and day out, by sitting on
park benches, even looking through cutout

00:06:01.270 --> 00:06:07.139
holes in newspapers, and wearing fake outfits
so as not to arouse suspicion.

00:06:07.139 --> 00:06:11.180
Steadily over time, the statue appeared to
gain either a heightened mobility or just

00:06:11.180 --> 00:06:13.030
a renewed sense of confidence.

00:06:13.030 --> 00:06:18.230
While much of the time it did remain standing
immobile, it would begin to occasionally stretch

00:06:18.230 --> 00:06:23.110
when it thought no one was looking and glance
this way and that in apparent annoyance with

00:06:23.110 --> 00:06:25.510
the birds circling over its head.

00:06:25.510 --> 00:06:28.160
The shootings steadily grew more regular.

00:06:28.160 --> 00:06:32.070
Foundation agents observed several birds being
picked out of the sky by the musket fire of

00:06:32.070 --> 00:06:35.220
SCP-011 over the following weeks.

00:06:35.220 --> 00:06:40.180
A clear pattern started to emerge: the statue
would only fire at birds that seemed to be

00:06:40.180 --> 00:06:43.169
flying above it or getting too curious about
it.

00:06:43.169 --> 00:06:48.530
In fact, the more fecal matter built up on
the statue, the more aggressive it would be.

00:06:48.530 --> 00:06:53.720
Both its body language and mood seemed to
sour the dirtier it got.

00:06:53.720 --> 00:06:57.900
While there were initial concerns about the
SCP potentially turning its rifle towards

00:06:57.900 --> 00:07:03.590
the local townspeople, these worries were
largely dismissed as SCP-011 gradually started

00:07:03.590 --> 00:07:06.200
to build up a rapport with those around it.

00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:10.960
Before long, the caretakers of the park were
having exchanges with the SCP.

00:07:10.960 --> 00:07:15.940
These exchanges started with the caretakers
speaking directly to the SCP and it nodding

00:07:15.940 --> 00:07:20.639
or subtly acknowledging the things they said,
but over time, the interactions grew more

00:07:20.639 --> 00:07:22.460
and more personable.

00:07:22.460 --> 00:07:26.990
In the year 2000, SCP-011 spoke for the first
time.

00:07:26.990 --> 00:07:32.020
It had just fired its rifle, picking off a
pigeon from over 200 feet away, when a caretaker

00:07:32.020 --> 00:07:34.230
mildly exclaimed, "Nice shot."

00:07:34.230 --> 00:07:40.539
The statue smiled, dipped his hat to the caretaker,
and said, "Thank you," in a gravelly voice.

00:07:40.539 --> 00:07:45.750
This marked a significant change in The Foundation's
approach to the containment of SCP-011.

00:07:45.750 --> 00:07:51.470
Up until this point, the SCP was considered
a broadly harmless member of the local town

00:07:51.470 --> 00:07:52.470
community.

00:07:52.470 --> 00:07:57.449
However, its ability to speak raised concerns
as to this SCP's development.

00:07:57.449 --> 00:08:01.890
Four years ago, it had been an immobile statue
with nothing out of the ordinary to raise

00:08:01.890 --> 00:08:04.620
any suspicions among those around it.

00:08:04.620 --> 00:08:07.500
Where would its cognitive development end?

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:13.330
Now it had gained the ability to talk, groundskeepers
and agents posing as groundskeepers struck

00:08:13.330 --> 00:08:17.080
up conversations with SCP-011 as often as
possible.

00:08:17.080 --> 00:08:23.280
At first, these exchanges were brief, but
over time, the SCP became steadily more vocal

00:08:23.280 --> 00:08:28.070
until soon it was engaged in intellectual
debates and sharing its views on the world

00:08:28.070 --> 00:08:29.720
with anyone who would listen.

00:08:29.720 --> 00:08:33.680
It was becoming clear that new containment
measures were needed.

00:08:33.680 --> 00:08:37.360
In fact, SCP-011 soon lost interest in shooting
birds.

00:08:37.360 --> 00:08:41.500
Or rather, the SCP was persuaded to stop shooting
birds.

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:46.610
While the prospect of having animals defecate
on it still appeared to anger the statue,

00:08:46.610 --> 00:08:51.180
The Foundation was able to explain, through
ideological grounds, why shooting birds was

00:08:51.180 --> 00:08:55.970
a disproportionate response relative to the
minor harm they were doing to it.

00:08:55.970 --> 00:09:01.640
Keen to engage in philosophical and ethical
discussions, the statue was very open to hearing

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:06.089
The Foundation's viewpoint on the issue, and
having sufficiently considered all sides of

00:09:06.089 --> 00:09:10.760
the debate, decided that it would, in fact,
be better for the well-being of all involved

00:09:10.760 --> 00:09:13.890
if it stopped shooting the birds from the
sky.

00:09:13.890 --> 00:09:18.510
In return, the caretakers and Foundation agents
promised to do their best to clean it regularly

00:09:18.510 --> 00:09:20.200
and keep the animals at bay.

00:09:20.200 --> 00:09:24.930
But with word of this bizarre tourist attraction
steadily gathering momentum as the age of

00:09:24.930 --> 00:09:30.730
email began to take off, The Foundation decided
that it would be best to relocate SCP-011

00:09:30.730 --> 00:09:31.870
entirely.

00:09:31.870 --> 00:09:36.339
However, agents who had been living in Woodstock
for the prior four years were hesitant to

00:09:36.339 --> 00:09:40.390
relocate the entity to a test chamber or storage
facility.

00:09:40.390 --> 00:09:44.820
The benefits that it had brought to the local
community far outweighed the risks and threats

00:09:44.820 --> 00:09:46.100
that it posed.

00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:51.320
The statue had become a local celebrity, smiling
and waving at children who went past, and

00:09:51.320 --> 00:09:55.570
even offering brief history lessons to any
confused tourists who found themselves wandering

00:09:55.570 --> 00:09:56.590
through the park.

00:09:56.590 --> 00:09:59.740
Most just assumed it was a person in gray
paint.

00:09:59.740 --> 00:10:05.980
It was Agent Khan who came up with the idea
of relocating SCP-011 to a museum.

00:10:05.980 --> 00:10:11.570
Being kept indoors away from the dangers of
any fecal bombing runs was the main priority.

00:10:11.570 --> 00:10:16.410
Khan argued that within a museum, the statue
would blend in seamlessly with the exhibits

00:10:16.410 --> 00:10:17.410
around it.

00:10:17.410 --> 00:10:21.610
Furthermore, if anyone did see the statue
move or talk, they would assume that it was

00:10:21.610 --> 00:10:25.160
an interactive exhibit and treated it as such.

00:10:25.160 --> 00:10:30.890
Having shown a real love for academia, history,
and debate, Khan believed that SCP-011 would

00:10:30.890 --> 00:10:35.639
benefit greatly from being in such a setting,
both learning and eventually even teaching

00:10:35.639 --> 00:10:38.459
about the history of the American Civil War.

00:10:38.459 --> 00:10:43.770
However, when all of these arguments were
put forward to the statue itself, it was hesitant.

00:10:43.770 --> 00:10:48.370
Having spent the entirety of its cognitive
existence standing on the same plinth, shooting

00:10:48.370 --> 00:10:54.940
at the same pigeons, the idea of relocating
to somewhere new and unknown was very intimidating.

00:10:54.940 --> 00:11:00.430
Even with the soldier's mindset, SCP-011 was
still feeling incredibly nervous about the

00:11:00.430 --> 00:11:02.899
idea of moving house.

00:11:02.899 --> 00:11:07.260
Agent Khan and SCP-011 found themselves locked
in a stalemate.

00:11:07.260 --> 00:11:11.960
Try as she might, convincing the SCP to leave
its current home was like talking to a brick

00:11:11.960 --> 00:11:14.830
wall, or rather, a stone wall.

00:11:14.830 --> 00:11:19.670
The pair of them ended up dropping the conversation
for a couple of years, focusing instead on

00:11:19.670 --> 00:11:23.709
psychiatric evaluations and history lessons
for the SCP.

00:11:23.709 --> 00:11:29.930
In 2002, the Foundation officially declared
that SCP-011 had achieved sentience with a

00:11:29.930 --> 00:11:34.860
great enough level of self-awareness to pass
as a normal human being, aside from the fact

00:11:34.860 --> 00:11:37.430
that it was composed entirely of stone.

00:11:37.430 --> 00:11:43.350
For two years, Agent Khan talked to SCP-011
every day on the park bench.

00:11:43.350 --> 00:11:46.870
The slats of the bench had to be replaced
several times as the weight of the statue

00:11:46.870 --> 00:11:51.589
broke through them, snapping them clean in
half on several occasions.

00:11:51.589 --> 00:11:56.130
During this period, the pair of them built
up a rapport rarely seen between humans and

00:11:56.130 --> 00:11:57.500
SCPs.

00:11:57.500 --> 00:12:04.760
So much so that in 2004, Agent Khan managed
to convince SCP-011 to move to a local museum

00:12:04.760 --> 00:12:07.970
on one condition: she would go as well.

00:12:07.970 --> 00:12:11.959
The Foundation agreed to the terms, deciding
that Khan could take on the role of being

00:12:11.959 --> 00:12:13.600
a researcher in the museum.

00:12:13.600 --> 00:12:19.630
That way, she could keep an eye on SCP-011
and report any activities while the Foundation

00:12:19.630 --> 00:12:22.910
officially relinquished control over the SCP.

00:12:22.910 --> 00:12:28.149
What happened next was perhaps rather predictable,
or at least it would be predictable to anyone

00:12:28.149 --> 00:12:33.230
who had worked with Agent Khan and SCP-011
during that time in Vermont.

00:12:33.230 --> 00:12:38.260
As the pair of them moved into their new lives
at the museum, romantic feelings blossomed

00:12:38.260 --> 00:12:39.430
between them.

00:12:39.430 --> 00:12:45.160
Seeing as SCP-011 is officially outside of
the SCP Foundation's jurisdiction, there has

00:12:45.160 --> 00:12:51.449
been no official inquiry into the nature - and
practicalities - of the relationship between

00:12:51.449 --> 00:12:53.510
the women and the statue.

00:12:53.510 --> 00:12:57.529
But from the reports that make their way to
the Foundation every three months, it is clear

00:12:57.529 --> 00:13:02.190
that both are very much enjoying the privacy
of their new arrangement.

00:13:02.190 --> 00:13:03.190
*

00:13:03.190 --> 00:13:07.140
Roger Pascal closed his eyes, imagining the
barrel raising higher and higher until it

00:13:07.140 --> 00:13:08.820
was pointed squarely at his face.

00:13:08.820 --> 00:13:13.100
He had been told by his bosses not to ask
questions about the origins of the statue

00:13:13.100 --> 00:13:16.180
that had suddenly appeared in the Civil War
section.

00:13:16.180 --> 00:13:20.180
Even when he saw the statue’s eyes moving,
he’d kept his mouth shut.

00:13:20.180 --> 00:13:24.830
That was until he was doing his security rounds
that night and heard those booming footsteps

00:13:24.830 --> 00:13:26.550
leading him behind one of the displays.

00:13:26.550 --> 00:13:28.910
He had rushed over in a panic.

00:13:28.910 --> 00:13:33.380
Peering around the corner, he had been shocked
to see Miss Khan, one of the researchers here,

00:13:33.380 --> 00:13:37.000
and the Civil War statue engaged in a passionate
kiss.

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:41.949
He had turned and bolted as fast as he could
until he ended up here, terrified on the floor

00:13:41.949 --> 00:13:44.839
as he imagined the musket being leveled at
him.

00:13:44.839 --> 00:13:48.870
But then a second pair of footsteps joined
the group, and a woman's laugh filled the

00:13:48.870 --> 00:13:49.870
room.

00:13:49.870 --> 00:13:54.390
Opening his eyes, the security guard saw the
pair of them, the statue and the researcher,

00:13:54.390 --> 00:13:58.050
standing in the doorway, laughing about the
whole situation.

00:13:58.050 --> 00:14:03.190
The musket was slung over the man's shoulder
as he offered a cold, stony hand down to the

00:14:03.190 --> 00:14:05.269
security guard to help him up.

00:14:05.269 --> 00:14:09.690
Ironically there was something about the statue’s
smile that softened Roger’s stoney heart

00:14:09.690 --> 00:14:11.800
as he was hauled to his feet.

00:14:11.800 --> 00:14:14.230
‘I have… so many questions.’

00:14:14.230 --> 00:14:21.600
Now check out “SCP-173 Origin Story - How
173 Got to Site-19” and “SCP-1913 Deadly

00:14:21.600 --> 00:14:23.459
Monster Squad - The Furies!”

